3.2 Asset Allocation & Total Portfolio Duties: 
• Conduct periodic asset allocation and asset-liability studies;
• Conduct annual asset allocation reviews and provide corresponding asset allocation 
recommendations addressing relevant risk and return parameters;
• Provide asset class research, analysis, and recommendations;
• Provide an annual liquidity review based on portfolio investment allocations and 
projected cash flows;
• Provide recommendations concerning investment manager allocation and structure;
• Provide recommendations concerning risk management strategies;
• Advise on the allocation of active and passive strategies;
• Provide access to analytical software and tools (as available) 
• Provide recommendations concerning securities lending strategies, and
periodic evaluation of and compliance monitoring for the MERF’s securities 
lending program;
• Provide periodic evaluation of and recommendations concerning custodial
arrangements, specifically custodian search and review services;
• Provide investment professional fee negotiation services;
• Provide recommendations concerning portfolio rebalancing and brokerage issues,
including directed brokerage, and transition manager services.
